---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from 'astrowind:config';
import JsonLd from '~/components/common/JsonLd.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: `SUP with Kids — ${SITE.name}`,
  description:
    'Family paddling guide: age recommendations, safety gear for children, kid-friendly boards, tips for keeping young paddlers engaged.',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <JsonLd
    type="Article"
    article={{
      headline: 'SUP with Kids',
      description:
        'Family paddling guide: age recommendations, safety gear for children, kid-friendly boards, tips for keeping young paddlers engaged.',
      datePublished: '2025-01-01',
    }}
    data={{ url: 'https://paddleboardoverstock.com/guides/sup-with-kids' }}
  />
  <JsonLd
    type="HowTo"
    howto={{
      name: 'SUP with Kids',
      description:
        'Family paddling guide: age recommendations, safety gear, kid-friendly boards, and tips for keeping young paddlers engaged.',
      steps: [
        {
          name: 'Age Recommendations',
          text: "Ages 3-6 ride on an adult's SUP. Ages 7-10 can paddle their own in calm water with supervision. Ages 11+ ready for full-size boards.",
        },
        {
          name: 'Safety Gear for Kids',
          text: 'A properly fitted life vest is mandatory. The vest should fit snugly. A leash should attach to a quick-release belt, not the child directly.',
        },
        {
          name: 'Best Boards for Families',
          text: 'The SUP Explorer 11 provides a stable platform for adult plus child.',
        },
        {
          name: 'Making It Fun',
          text: 'Keep trips short — 30-45 minutes. Incorporate games, bring snacks, and let children help with setup to build excitement.',
        },
        {
          name: 'Choosing the Right Environment',
          text: 'Start on small, sheltered lakes with sandy beaches. Avoid strong currents and heavy water traffic. Choose days with wind under 8 mph.',
        },
        {
          name: 'Teaching Water Safety',
          text: "Review basic safety rules before each trip: stay seated, wear the life vest, stay within arm's reach, and know what to do if they fall in.",
        },
      ],
    }}
  />
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-24 px-6" data-ai-block="definition">
    <a href="/guides" class="text-sm text-sky-600 hover:text-sky-700">→Guides</a>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold text-gray-900">SUP with Kids</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-500">
      Introducing children to paddling creates lifelong outdoor enthusiasts. Here is how to do it safely.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-12">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Age Recommendations</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">
          Ages 3-6: ride on an adult's SUP with a parent. Ages 7-10: can paddle their own small SUP in calm, shallow
          water with close supervision. Ages 11+: ready for full-size boards with proper instruction. Every child
          develops differently — assess confidence and swimming ability before introducing paddling.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Safety Gear for Kids</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">
          A properly fitted life vest is mandatory for children. Choose a vest rated for your child's weight and
          approved for their size. The vest should fit snugly — lift the shoulders to check; the vest should not ride up
          over the chin. A leash is essential and should be attached to a quick-release belt, not the child directly.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Best Boards for Families</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">
          The SUP Explorer 11 (32-inch width) provides a stable platform for an adult with a child on the nose. For
          older children ready to paddle independently, a lightweight all-around board is easy for a pre-teen to carry
          and launch.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Making It Fun</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">
          Keep trips short — 30-45 minutes is plenty for young children. Incorporate games: follow the leader, paddle to
          a specific buoy and back, or look for wildlife. Bring snacks in a dry bag. Let children help with setup and
          inflation — involving them in the process builds ownership and excitement. End the trip before they get tired
          or bored.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Choosing the Right Environment</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">
          Start on small, sheltered lakes with no water traffic. Sandy beaches with gradual entry are ideal — no sharp
          rocks or shells. Avoid areas with strong currents, navigation channels, or steep drop-offs. Check the forecast
          and choose days with wind under 8 mph and no thunderstorm risk. The calmer the conditions, the more fun
          everyone will have.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Teaching Water Safety</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">
          Before each trip, review basic safety rules: stay seated or kneeling until comfortable, always wear the life
          vest, stay within arm's reach of an adult, what to do if they fall in (stay calm, hold the board). Make safety
          a habit from the very first outing — children who learn safety early become responsible paddlers as adults.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 p-6 bg-sky-50 rounded-2xl border border-sky-100">
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Related</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
        <a
          href="/guides/safety-tips"
          class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 hover:border-sky-300"
          >Safety Tips</a
        >
        <a
          href="/guides/beginner-guide"
          class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 hover:border-sky-300"
          >Beginner Guide</a
        >
        <a
          href="/guides/choosing-paddle"
          class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 hover:border-sky-300"
          >Choosing a Paddle</a
        >
        <a
          href="/products?category=INFLATABLE"
          class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 hover:border-sky-300"
          >Shop SUP Boards</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>
</Layout>
